<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Mentio collects, uses, and protects your data."
  updated="August 3, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Mentio ("we", "us") is a social listening service for developer platforms, available at
    <a href="https://mentio.dev">mentio.dev</a>. This policy explains what data we collect, why we
    collect it, and the choices you have. Questions or requests: write to
    <a href="mailto:support@mentio.dev">support@mentio.dev</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Data you give us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account data.</strong> Your name, email address, and a password (stored only as a
      salted hash) when you sign up, or your Google account identity if you sign in with Google.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Workspace data.</strong> The keywords you track, your company profile and context,
      feed and notification settings, and anything else you configure in the product.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Integration credentials.</strong> If you connect Slack, we store the workspace name,
      ids, and the bot token Slack issues so we can post notifications to the channel you pick.
      Disconnecting removes the token and we ask Slack to revoke it. API keys you mint are stored
      only as hashes and are shown to you once.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data we collect automatically</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Usage and billing counters.</strong> Active keyword counts and relevant mention
      counts per billing cycle, which determine your bill.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service logs.</strong> Standard operational logs (timestamps, request metadata,
      errors) kept for reliability and abuse prevention.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use <strong>essential cookies only</strong>: a session cookie to keep you signed in. No
    advertising or cross-site tracking cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>Public content we process</h2>
  <p>
    The product works by monitoring publicly available posts on platforms such as Bluesky, Hacker
    News, Reddit, X, GitHub, Stack Overflow, DEV, YouTube, and news sources. For matched posts we
    store the public text, link, and author handle, and classify them with AI (relevance,
    sentiment, intent) so you can filter your feed. This is public data, processed to provide the
    service. If a post is deleted at its source it may persist in our index; authors can request
    removal at <a href="mailto:support@mentio.dev">support@mentio.dev</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use data</h2>
  <p>
    To provide and improve the service, deliver the notifications you configure, bill usage,
    secure the platform, and communicate with you about your account. We do not sell personal
    data and we do not run ads. AI classification runs on Cloudflare Workers AI; we do not use
    your data or monitored content to train our own models.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: hosting, storage, and AI inference for the entire service.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Polar</strong>: our merchant of record. Payments, invoices, and card details are
      handled by Polar; we never see or store your payment card data.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Slack</strong>: only if you connect it, to post notifications you configure.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong>: only if you choose Google sign-in.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Account and workspace data is kept while your account is active and deleted when you ask us
    to close it. Billing records are kept as long as law requires. Monitored public posts live in
    a shared index; deleting your account removes your organization's associations with them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    If you are in the EU/EEA (GDPR) or a similar jurisdiction, you can request access,
    correction, deletion, portability, or restriction of your personal data, and object to
    processing, by emailing <a href="mailto:support@mentio.dev">support@mentio.dev</a>. You can
    also lodge a complaint with your local supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    All traffic is encrypted in transit. Passwords and API keys are stored hashed, integration
    tokens are scoped to the minimum permissions the feature needs, and access to production data
    is restricted.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this policy as the service evolves and change the date above. Material changes
    will be announced in the product or by email.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
